# Env files. GEMINI_API_KEY lives in ai-backend/.env and must never be
# committed; AI_API_URL lives in the root .env. A pattern with no slash matches
# at any depth, so these two lines cover both without naming either path.
.env
.env*.local
.env.*
# ...but the committed templates have to stay visible. This negation is
# ORDER-DEPENDENT: it only re-includes a file because it is written after
# `.env.*`, and git takes the last matching pattern. Moving it above the
# `.env*` lines silently hides ai-backend/.env.example — a missing template
# reads as "nothing to copy" rather than as a broken ignore rule.
!.env.example
!.env.sample

